    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "1.4. Connection to Gaussian multiplicative chaos. We now explain the connection between our variance (which we think of as mean squares of random Euler products like (1.2)) and the theory of Gaussian multiplicative chaos, restricting ourselves to the Steinhaus case. For an introduction to the theory, see Rhodes and Vargas [29]. A similar discussion can be found in the introduction of Harper [15]. Here, we put a particular emphasis on understanding the limiting distribution of our variances."
